  The portMirror line is the one that matters: REPLACE_TRUTH_VALUE is set,
  which means the flag setup ran. Under the plan's header-only reading it
  would read 0 and Task 7 would silently convert nothing.

  The test builds for the host so it can actually be run, from the same source
  and the same -D set as the target library. Host and target differ in the
  width of net-snmp's oid typedef, which changes struct layout but not which
  entries exist or what they say.

